{
  "_id": "tg-disobedience",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "because ye would not be obedient, Deut. 8:20 (28:62). curse, if ye will not obey the commandments, Deut. 11:28. rebellious son … will not obey the voice of his father, Deut. 21:18 (21:18–21). consumed, because they obeyed not, Josh. 5:6. ye have not obeyed my voice, Judg. 2:2 (6:10; Jer. 9:13; 18:10; 22:21). people refused to obey the voice of Samuel, 1 Sam. 8:19. if ye will not obey the voice of the Lord, 1 Sam. 12:15. thou hast rejected the word of the Lord, 1 Sam. 15:23 (Jer. 8:9). thou hast disobeyed the mouth of the Lord, 1 Kgs. 13:21. Because they obeyed not the voice of the Lord, 2 Kgs. 18:12. they were disobedient, and rebelled against thee, Neh. 9:26. if they obey not, they shall perish by the sword, Job 36:12. I have called, and ye refused, Prov. 1:24. have not obeyed the voice of my teachers, Prov. 5:13. they have transgressed the laws, Isa. 24:5. neither were they obedient unto his law, Isa. 42:24. Only acknowledge … ye have not obeyed my voice, Jer. 3:13. Cursed be the man that obeyeth not the words, Jer. 11:3. if they will not obey, I will utterly pluck up, Jer. 12:17. declared it to you; but ye have not obeyed, Jer. 42:21. sinned … and have not obeyed the voice, Jer. 44:23. Israel … might not obey thy voice, Dan. 9:11. our God is righteous in all his works … for we obeyed not, Dan. 9:14. because thou hast rejected knowledge, Hosea 4:6. She obeyed not the voice, Zeph. 3:2.",
