    {
      "text": "to turn … the disobedient to the wisdom of the just, Luke 1:17. call … Lord, Lord, and do not the things which I say, Luke 6:46. To whom our fathers would not obey, Acts 7:39. have received the law … and have not kept it, Acts 7:53. I was not disobedient unto the heavenly vision, Acts 26:19. despiteful … disobedient to parents, Rom. 1:30 (2 Tim. 3:2). contentious, and do not obey the truth, Rom. 2:8. by one man’s disobedience many were made sinners, Rom. 5:19. stretched forth my hands unto a disobedient … people, Rom. 10:21. having in a readiness to revenge all disobedience, 2 Cor. 10:6. who did hinder you that ye should not obey the truth, Gal. 5:7. spirit that … worketh in the children of disobedience, Eph. 2:2. wrath of God upon the children of disobedience, Eph. 5:6 (Col. 3:6). vengeance on them that … obey not the gospel, 2 Thes. 1:8. the law is … for the lawless and disobedient, 1 Tim. 1:9. deny him, being abominable, and disobedient, Titus 1:16. we ourselves also were sometimes foolish, disobedient, Titus 3:3. disobedience received a just recompence, Heb. 2:2. unto them which be disobedient, the stone, 1 Pet. 2:7. husbands … if any obey not the word, 1 Pet. 3:1. Which sometime were disobedient, 1 Pet. 3:20 (D&C 138:9, 28). what shall the end be of them that obey not the gospel, 1 Pet. 4:17.",
